{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>The El of Beit El.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, is in Beit El — the revelation of His Shekhinah in Beit El. There is a word missing a bet serving as its prefix, as in ״הִנֵּה הוּא בֵּית מָכִיר בֶּן עַמִּיאֵל״ (II Samuel 9) — like בְּבֵית מָכִיר; ״בֵּית אָבִיךָ״ (Genesis 38:11) — like בְּבֵית אָבִיךָ." "<b>And the Elohim were revealed to him.</b> In many places the divine name of Elohim and Adonai appear in the plural, as in ״אֲדֹנֵי יוֹסֵף״ (Genesis 39), ״אִם בְּעָלָיו עִמּוֹ״ (Exodus 20) — and it does not say בַּעֲלוֹ; and likewise the name Elohim, which is a term of judging and dominion, is recalled in the plural — but any of the other names you will not find in the plural."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:02:10.445416500Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}